Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns & potential usage
• primary_type: filter rows where the crime category is ‘MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT’.  
• date: extract the calendar month via EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) for month–level grouping.  
• year: filter the period 2010‑2016 and use for per‑year aggregation.  

Typical conditions  
• WHERE primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'  
• AND year BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016  

Ten step‑by‑step exploration queries
```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at distinct crime categories to make sure the spelling of “MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT” exists.
SELECT DISTINCT primary_type
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
ORDER BY primary_type
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Show a handful of motor‑vehicle‑theft rows (2010‑2016) to see the date and year columns.
SELECT unique_key, primary_type, date, year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
WHERE primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
  AND year BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Count total motor thefts per year in the requested range.
SELECT year, COUNT(*) AS motor_thefts
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
WHERE primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
  AND year BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Add the calendar month to see how many thefts occur each month.
SELECT year,
       EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS month,
       COUNT(*) AS motor_thefts
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
WHERE primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
  AND year BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016
GROUP BY year, month
ORDER BY year, month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) For one specific year (2010) list all monthly counts to inspect distribution.
SELECT EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS month,
       COUNT(*) AS motor_thefts_2010
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
WHERE primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
  AND year = 2010
GROUP BY month
ORDER BY motor_thefts_2010 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Introduce a window function to compute the max monthly total for every year.
SELECT year,
       EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS month,
       COUNT(*) AS motor_thefts,
       MAX(COUNT(*)) OVER (PARTITION BY year) AS max_monthly_thefts_per_year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
WHERE primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
  AND year BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016
GROUP BY year, month
ORDER BY year, month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Keep only the months that actually hit the yearly maximum (ties possible).
WITH monthly AS (
  SELECT year,
         EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS month,
         COUNT(*) AS motor_thefts
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
  WHERE primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
    AND year BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016
  GROUP BY year, month
), ranked AS (
  SELECT *,
         RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY year ORDER BY motor_thefts DESC) AS rnk
  FROM monthly
)
SELECT year, month, motor_thefts
FROM ranked
WHERE rnk = 1
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Same as #7 but show the month name for readability.
WITH monthly AS (
  SELECT year,
         EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS month_num,
         COUNT(*) AS motor_thefts
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
  WHERE primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
    AND year BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016
  GROUP BY year, month_num
), ranked AS (
  SELECT *,
         RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY year ORDER BY motor_thefts DESC) AS rnk
  FROM monthly
)
SELECT year,
       FORMAT_DATE('%B', DATE_FROM_UNIX_DATE(30*month_num)) AS month_name,
       motor_thefts
FROM ranked
WHERE rnk = 1
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Aggregate two metrics—max monthly total and the overall yearly total—to compare scale.
WITH monthly AS (
  SELECT year,
         EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS month,
         COUNT(*) AS motor_thefts
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
  WHERE primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
    AND year BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016
  GROUP BY year, month
)
SELECT year,
       MAX(motor_thefts) AS max_monthly_motor_thefts,
       SUM(motor_thefts) AS total_year_motor_thefts
FROM monthly
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) FINAL ANSWER QUERY – highest number of motor‑vehicle thefts that occurred in any single month for each year 2010‑2016.
WITH monthly AS (
  SELECT year,
         EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS month,
         COUNT(*) AS motor_thefts
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
  WHERE primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
    AND year BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016
  GROUP BY year, month
)
SELECT year,
       MAX(motor_thefts) AS max_motor_thefts_in_one_month
FROM monthly
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

